<section class="report-section" id="update-freshness">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">Section 04</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Retailer Reporting Freshness Analysis</h2>
  </div>

  <p>Update lag measures the time between when a retailer last updated their price in the government feed (<code>source_updated_at</code>) and when it was captured by the data collection system (<code>recorded_at</code>). A lag of near-zero indicates a live, up-to-date price; large lags indicate stale data that may misrepresent what a consumer would actually pay on arrival.</p>

  <p>This analysis covers <strong>48,989 records</strong> with non-negative lags. The 1,011 records (2.0%) where <code>source_updated_at</code> falls <em>after</em> <code>recorded_at</code> are anomalous (possible clock-skew) and are excluded.</p>

